Evaluation can score frozen probabilities against a different handicap, and metadata replay does not bind the parser implementation provenance. No full test suites were rerun.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Validate evaluation handicaps against frozen forecast inputs — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/r/fm171_26103_evaluate.R:19-21
  If the roster is corrected after freezing forecasts, evaluation silently uses its new handicap to construct outcomes while probabilities still describe the original handicap. The replay checks cover forecast files, not the newly opened roster, so they cannot detect this mismatch. Compare evaluation fixture identities and handicaps against the frozen inputs and reject mismatches before scoring. This enforces the boundary validation requirement in [AGENTS.md:52–57](AGENTS.md#L52-L57).

- [P2] Bind metadata parser implementations into the replay receipt — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/src/fm171_26103_metadata.py:53-53
  The metadata receipt hashes this client and the input JSON, but not the imported `analysis_record`, `parse_opponent_history`, or their implementation dependencies. Changing those implementations without changing their output leaves metadata replay successful and downstream metadata bindings unchanged, despite changing the code that establishes competition and venue eligibility. Include transitive parser implementation hashes in the frozen body and replay comparison, as required by [AGENTS.md:136](AGENTS.md#L136).
